    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772-a2">

                <pb facs="0728" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg630"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander Moser to
                        Mr. Bowers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. Commission of Fish and Fisheries, Steamer Albatross</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Suva Harbor Fiji Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                10, 1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: During our brief visit to Nuku’Alofa,
                    Tonga, where we have no diplomatic or consular representative, Her Britannic
                    Majesty’s deputy commissioner and vice consul, Mr. R. Beckwith Leefe, placed his
                    services at our disposition, and through him an audience was arranged and held
                    with King George Turbou II. If you deem it proper the Department of State might
                    be notified and the service acknowledged to the British Government.</p>
                <p>The audience was formed of three officers, Mr. Woodworth, who accompanied Mr.
                    Agassiz, and myself. We were received by the King and his ministers, and after
                    some questions and explanations as to the nature of our work and expressions of
                    good will we retired.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jeff. F. Moser</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commander United States Navy,
                        Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
